  "notes": "Sequence transcribed from the official Program Guide PDF (Program Guide link on the official program page, anokatech.edu/programs/scoping-proofreading/; https://www.anokatech.edu/media/xmmhmd2l/scoping-proofreading-certificate.pdf, retrieved 2026-10-01). The PDF template header prints '2023-2024'; the guide is the currently published program guide and its program name, sequence, and 29-credit total match the current official programs listing (Scoping/Proofreading Certificate, 29 credits). The 29-credit program is designed to be completed in one-and-a-half years. Scoping/Proofreading students learn shorthand theory with Judicial Reporting students and also take Legal Terminology, Medical Terminology, Realtime Reporting Orientation, Realtime Reporting Technology, Business English and Transcription and English courses; the three additional required classes are Advanced Proofreading and English Skills, Scoping Procedures and Advanced Transcript Production. All courses required for this program must be completed with a grade of C or higher. Program starts Fall (August) and Spring (January). Laptop, steno machine, and Case CATalyst student or professional software are required; see instructor for specific requirements before purchasing.",
